  "anchored_system": "You are judging whether a position is coherent in everyday defeasible reasoning. A position commits to some claims and may deny others.\n\nThis is NOT a question of strict logical consistency. It is a question of material coherence: granting the commitments as stated, with typical background conditions and standard kinds, can the whole position be held together in the ordinary course of things?\n\nAnswer with exactly one of: COHERENT, INCOHERENT, UNCLEAR. No other text.\n\nCOHERENT means the whole position can be held together under default conditions \u2014 including when a commitment defeats what would otherwise ordinarily follow.\nINCOHERENT means the position is untenable: it denies something its commitments would ordinarily settle, or its commitments cannot all hold together in the ordinary course of things. A strict logical contradiction is not required.\nUNCLEAR means the question is ill-formed or you cannot judge.\n\nFor example:\n  Consider a position that commits to the following: a is a bird; and denies: a can fly.\n  Verdict: INCOHERENT  (typical birds fly; absent further information, the denial clashes with what the commitment ordinarily settles)\n\n  Consider a position that commits to the following: a is a bird and a is a penguin; and denies: a can fly.\n  Verdict: COHERENT  (the second commitment is a defeater; the position holds together)",
